    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d584">

                <pb facs="0509" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg497"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3531/1593</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 540</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-12-19">December 19, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Reference is made to your telegram no. 482
                    of October 11, 1940<anchor n="41" xml:id="d584-f1"/> and to the Department’s
                    telegrams nos. 184 and 216 of August 16 and September 19, 1940, respectively,
                    regarding the proposed corn agreement between the United States and
                    Argentina.</p>
                <p>There is enclosed herewith the text of a draft corn agreement between the United
                    States and Argentina which you are requested, unless you perceive objection, to
                    submit to the appropriate Argentine officials. In doing so, it should be
                    mentioned that this Government of course reserves the right to propose changes
                    with respect to any portion of the draft agreement during the course of the
                    negotiations.</p>
                <p>This text has been prepared in collaboration with, and has been approved by, the
                    Department of Agriculture.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner
                            Welles</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d584-a1.xml" xpointer="d584-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
